  "question": {
    "text": "A hollow cylindrical conductor has length of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>, while its inner and outer diameters are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math> respectively. The resistance of the conductor is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#937;</mi></math>.<br />If the resistivity of the material is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#937;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></math> is _____."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Resistance of a conductor with uniform cross-section is given by,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#961;</mi><mfrac><mi>l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mfrac></math></p><p>In this case&nbsp;the cross-sectional area is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#960;</mi><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p><p>Therefore,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#961;</mi><mfrac><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn mathvariant=\"italic\">2</mn></msup><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">-</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn mathvariant=\"italic\">2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mfenced><mrow><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#937;</mi></math></p><p>Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>.</p>"
  }
}